  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="bf27-1d46-f658-a4ea" name="Swiss (Armies of Chivalry) - List Notes" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false">
      <description>THE SWISS 1422-1522 (Armies of Chivalry, p.57). Cantonal Standards: the Gewalthut must begin the game as the largest unit in the army (other units may be as large) and should contain one or more flags in addition to its unit standard. While the Gewalthut is in good order (neither destroyed, fleeing, nor off the table) all formed Swiss infantry units within 12" of it may re-roll failed Break tests. The Gewalthut gains an additional +1 combat results bonus as if it had an Army Standard. If it loses its standards to a victorious opponent, they are worth 300 Victory points. Command By Committee: no Swiss characters are used; pike and halberd units may purchase a Captain for 20 pts instead of a Leader. A Captain is treated as a unit leader and the unit may add +1 to its Leadership; his two attacks are always made at Strength 4.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[The Swiss]
  Infantry: at least 66%
  Cavalry/Support: up to 33%
  Infantry 66-100%, Cavalry/Support 0-33%. The Swiss have no Characters (Command by Committee).</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
